A||||7||Notchit||Removing bottom moldings on 85 GT||||5||
Z||000000||Notchit||12-27-2000||05:15 PM||||Hello,<BR>I am a new forum member  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, and Fiero owner. i've read through all your postings but couldn't find this topic. I have a 1985 Fiero GT, the side bottom molding has a hole in it, so it needs to be replaced. its not the door panel, but the bottom molding that runs from the front tire to the back. I drilled out the 8 or so rivits holding the piece to the car frame, but the top is still attached to the frame, and i am confused on how to get it off. please answer in detail if you can help me!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Thank-you!<P><BR>Ryan||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-27-2000||07:36 PM||||Inside the door jamb, notice 3 cover tabs (2 short and 1 long) Pop these off to reveal additional rivits to remove the same way.<BR>When removing from side of body there are 2 'snap' tabs into the front fender on the top and 3 on the rear quarter panel. <BR>No problems.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Notchit||12-27-2000||08:44 PM||||OK, i took of those three cover things, removed the rivits (which were a ***** ..) but now i'm trying to figure out how to remove those tab things, do I push them in or use a putty knife anf push upwards or what?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR>_________________________||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||12-27-2000||09:22 PM||||Take a screw driver (stright tip), insert on the top of tab in the center of tab and push the back of the tab down toward the floor. Wriggle it gently as you pull it away from the car.  Two in the front fender and three in the rear.<P>OH, and welcome to the forum!||||reg||11
Z||000004||Notchit||12-27-2000||09:30 PM||||Aww man thanks a lot, i've been trying to remove this thing for about a week, at it was getting on my nerves, thanks for the welcome as well, you'll see me on here very often!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Ryan||||reg||10
Z||000005||Notchit||12-27-2000||10:23 PM||||Alright, now I am taking off the molding that is attached to the door. when I look at the rivits there is peices sticking out, like nipples<P>________   &lt;--under door<BR> |_|| <P>Now, how do I remove these? i can't drill them, at least I don't think i can...thanks||209.197.150.117||reg||4
Z||000006||2xsess||12-28-2000||01:33 AM||||Use a punch and knock the center of the rivet in. It's not attached. Then you can drill out the rivet easily.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Notchit||12-28-2000||02:07 AM||||Done and Done!<BR>thanks you guys!<P>------------------<BR>Seein Red<BR>'85 Fiero GT<BR>ICQ#: 56708070<BR>_________________________||||reg||10
